From 98a152d6c846dae016839ab8c1f57e214687491b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:29:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: avs: cpr: Describe an MSM8926 sleep voter

Allow an optional independent MX sleep-only supplier on MSM8926. CPR
retains a covering ceiling while APC can remain live. Only a complete
system entry coordinator may later authorize a lower sleep floor after
quiescing CPR and establishing CPU/L2/RPM power-collapse ordering.

Codex generated this change and its host qualification. Human review and
DCO certification remain pending. Nothing has been submitted.

Backport this prerequisite to maintained Linux 6.18.63. The complete
seventeen-change batch passes native ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT object
builds with the MSM8926 feature enabled and disabled. CPU-idle is ARM
only. Host fault models use synthetic services and normal LeakSanitizer;
firmware, electrical and physical suspend acceptance remain open.

Codex prepared this local backport and verification. Original authors,
dates, licenses and human attribution tags are retained. Human DCO and
review remain pending. No phone access or publication occurred.

Backported from commit b72d674810b4 ("dt-bindings: power: avs: cpr:
Describe an MSM8926 sleep voter")
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/power/avs/qcom,cpr.yaml          | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/avs/qcom,cpr.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/avs/qcom,cpr.yaml
index b6e7b97f0654d..2352502742090 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/avs/qcom,cpr.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/avs/qcom,cpr.yaml
@@ -46,6 +46,14 @@ properties:
   vdd-mx-supply:
     description: Memory rail dependency of the MSM8926 APC supply.
 
+  vdd-mx-sleep-supply:
+    description:
+      Optional independent MSM8926 memory-rail sleep-only voter. CPR retains
+      an enabled request at its supported maximum while APC can remain live.
+      A complete system entry coordinator must quiesce CPR and establish the
+      CPU/L2/RPM power-collapse ordering before lowering this sleep request.
+      This voter must not contribute to the active set.
+
   '#power-domain-cells':
     const: 0
 
@@ -115,6 +123,7 @@ allOf:
           items:
             - const: ref
         vdd-mx-supply: false
+        vdd-mx-sleep-supply: false
         qcom,apcs-syscon: false
         nvmem-cells:
           items:
-- 
